Force at least one merge AND one split to exercise the full mutation
surface.

5.1 SETUP for the merge (intentionally seed a duplicate to consolidate):
    Have the github SME for `dream11/auth-svc` and the telemetry SME
    for `auth-svc` (catalog) BOTH write components for the same
    logical service. This is realistic — multi-plane discovery
    naturally produces apparent duplicates.

5.2 SIBLING SEARCH (Phase 10.7 default exclude_self=True):
    SMEs run vector_search on components with their own description
    as query. Phase 10.7 default skips own row → top results are
    real candidates. Verify in caveman chat: SME reports something
    like:
      "vector_search found peer auth-svc-tel (sim=0.91). nominate
      merge." (not "found self at top-1, skip, then peer").

5.3 NOMINATE MERGE: github SME nominates merge with telemetry SME's
    auth-svc component. b_conf converges → auto-escalate to R.

5.4 SYMMETRIC-NOMINATION RACE GUARD (Phase 10.1 + 10.1.1):
    Have a different SME attempt the REVERSE nomination
    (telemetry-side nominates github-side). Expected: blocked
    with "Open consolidation between these components already
    exists" (Phase 10.1 SELECT pre-check) OR PostgreSQL UNIQUE
    violation (Phase 10.1.1 partial UNIQUE index, fallback for
    microsecond race). Either is PASS.

5.5 RESOLVER REVIEW: r_conf ≥0.85 → status=M, mutation_assigned_to
    = pick richer side per the Absorber Pick (plane-coverage,
    attribution count, catalog count, doc_md length).

5.6 PRE-MERGE HANDOFF (mandatory):
    Survivor raises a clarification to absorbed-target asking for
    runtime knowledge NOT captured in component_doc_md / attributions
    / edges. Wait for QC. Capture answers in survivor's
    ./component_doc.md (workspace rule) THEN absorb.

5.7 EXECUTE MUTATION: absorb_agent (with cascade=true defaults).
    Verify: catalogs cascade BEFORE flows (Phase 7.4.2). Verify all
    cascaded counts in the response.

5.8 SPLIT NOMINATION: pick one SME (e.g. orders-svc) and have it
    nominate a split — claim the resource is actually 2 components.
    Resolver approves → M. mutation_assigned_to = self (always
    for splits).

